
                                Main Menu Help
                                --------------


T - Time

    Displays the current date and time, along with the amount of online
    time you have remaining.

B - Bulletins

    Takes you to the Bulletin Menu.  Here you can view a variety of text
    and information files posted to users by the SysOp.

Y - Yell at SysOp

    If you need to speak with the SysOp, use this command to page him.  If
    he is available, he will break in to chat with you.  Please only use
    this if you requires his immediate attention.  If you can just leave
    him a message then do so.

C - Change Setup

    Here you can edit information abuot yourself and change some settings
    that you use on the BBS.

F - File Areas

    This is where you can transfer files to and from the BBS.  Note that
    this is an Amiga BBS, so all files must be Amiga related.

O - Online Games

    Takes you to the online games menu, where there is a selection of
    games for users to play.

G - Good-Bye

    When you want to logoff of the board, use this command.  DO NOT DROP
    CARRIER OR YOUR ACCESS WILL BE LOWERED.

J - Join

    This is available to new users only.  If you decide you want to become
    a member of this BBS, then use this command and answer the questions
    HONESTLY.

M - Message Areas

    This is for the posting and reading of messages for other users to
    read.

U - User List

    Gives a listing of the users on the board.  Also allows you to search the
    user list for a specific string.

L - Leave Feedback

    This is just a quick way to leave a message to the SysOp.  New users
    especially are encouraged to leave the SysOp feedback.
    
V - Version Info

    Displays the current version of TransAmiga being used.

W - Who's Online?

    Lists who is on all the currently active BBS lines, and what they are
    doing.

! - Send Node Message

    Posts a message to another node, if any others are active.

